# <%= current_page.data.title %>

## General information

- Our team have a stand up each morning at 9:30.
- We plan our sprints using GitHub Projects.
- We have our team retrospective every 2 weeks at the end of each sprint.
- We have a backlog refinement session halfway through every sprint.

## Tools

### Communication

Our main chat platform is Slack, and this is our preferred method of communication.

Most catalogue related discussions take place in the main team channel: [#justice-data-platform-squad-2](https://moj.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C093NTY9JHE).

Automated updates (for example GitHub notifications) appear in [#find-moj-data](https://moj.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C03QZ776JVA)

Alerts are posted to [#find-moj-data-alerts-prod](https://moj.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C07SFN0MHRP)

Our [agile ceremonies](/documentation/ways-of-working#ceremonies) take place in MS teams,
making use of Miro boards for collecting feedback from the team,
or looking at the [team github projects board](https://github.com/orgs/ministryofjustice/projects/57/views/6) for planning.

Our main Slack channels are:

#### #justice-data-platform-squad-2

The [#justice-data-platform-squad-2](https://moj.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C093NTY9JHE) channel is our team channel,
where we have discussions about anything ranging from:

- technical issues
- user centered design
- questions or discussions around the service
- to request someone else from the team's help
- support rota notifications
- when we're away for lunch or some other appointment
- general musings

If you can't make standup, post your standup update here.

### GitHub

Access to Data Catalogue's GitHub repositories and projects is managed in Terraform.

To add a user to a team, add their GitHub username to the data-catalogue team in the
[`data-catalogue.tf`](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/data-platform-github-access/blob/main/data-catalogue.tf) configuration.
